astatine.options.view_distance.tooltip=The render distance controls how far away terrain will be rendered. Shorter distances mean that less terrain will be rendered, improving frame rates.
astatine.options.brightness.tooltip=Controls the brightness (gamma) of the game.
astatine.options.gui_scale.tooltip=Sets the maximum scale factor to be used for the user interface. If "auto" is used, then the largest scale factor will always be used.
astatine.options.fullscreen.tooltip=If enabled, the game will display in full-screen (if supported).
astatine.options.v_sync.tooltip=If enabled, the game's frame rate will be synchronized to the monitor's refresh rate, making for a generally smoother experience at the expense of overall input latency. This setting might reduce performance if your system is too slow.
astatine.options.fps_limit.tooltip=Limits the maximum number of frames per second. This can help reduce battery usage and system load when multi-tasking. If VSync is enabled, this option will be ignored unless it is lower than your display's refresh rate.
astatine.options.view_bobbing.tooltip=If enabled, the player's view will sway and bob when moving around. Players who experience motion sickness while playing may benefit from disabling this.
astatine.options.anaglyph.tooltip=Renders the game in red-cyan stereoscopic 3D for use with anaglyph glasses.
astatine.options.graphics_quality.tooltip=The default graphics quality controls some legacy options such as leaves and weather, and is necessary for mod compatibility.
astatine.options.clouds_quality.tooltip=The quality level used for rendering clouds in the sky. Even though the options are labeled "Fast" and "Fancy", the effect on performance is negligible.
astatine.options.particle_quality.tooltip=Controls the maximum number of particles which can be present on screen at any one time.
astatine.options.smooth_lighting.tooltip=Enables the smooth lighting and shading of blocks in the world. This can very slightly increase the amount of time it takes to load or update a chunk, but it doesn't affect frame rates.
astatine.options.entity_shadows.tooltip=If enabled, basic shadows will be rendered beneath mobs and other entities.
astatine.options.alternate_blocks.tooltip=If enabled, blocks with alternate models in the resource pack will pick a random variant.
astatine.options.mipmap_levels.tooltip=Controls the number of mipmaps which will be used for block model textures. Higher values provide better rendering of blocks in the distance, but could adversely affect performance with resource packs that use many animated textures.
astatine.options.chunk_update_threads.name=Chunk Update Threads
astatine.options.chunk_update_threads.tooltip=Specifies the number of threads to use for chunk building. Using more threads can speed up chunk loading and update speed, but may negatively impact frame times. The default value is usually good enough for all situations.
astatine.options.vbo.tooltip=Vanilla's vertex buffer object setting. Astatine always renders terrain through Vulkan buffers, so this only affects vanilla code paths.
astatine.options.shaders_enabled.name=Enable Shaders
astatine.options.shaders_enabled.tooltip=If enabled, the selected shader pack is used for rendering. Use the Shader Packs button to choose a pack.
astatine.options.allow_unknown_shaders.name=Allow Unknown Shaders
astatine.options.allow_unknown_shaders.tooltip=Allows core shaders that the shader pack doesn't know about to draw to the main color texture.
astatine.options.shader_debug.name=Shader Debug Mode
astatine.options.shader_debug.tooltip=Prints detailed shader compilation output and enables debug key bindings. This costs some performance.
